<abstract>
<para>Kernel control groups (cgroups) in &productname; provide a unified hierarchical framework to organize processes and regulate their consumption of system resources like CPU, memory, and I/O. Managed through systemd slices, cgroups v2 enable precise resource accounting and process isolation, preventing resource exhaustion and ensuring high-priority enterprise workloads remain stable and performant under heavy demand.</para>
  <para><emphasis role="bold">Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
  <itemizedlist>
    <listitem>
      <para>Btrfs, Ext4, or XFS file system to enable accurate background writeback tracking</para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
      <para>Active BFQ scheduler or IOCost on block devices for proportional I/O control</para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
      <para>Explicit controller delegation configured for systemd user session instances</para>
    </listitem>
  </itemizedlist>
</abstract>
